==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ru|orv|добръ}}, in turn from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*dòbrъ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|добро́}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-добро́.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|добро́|n=sg}}

# [[good]] (that which is ethical or moral, the opposite of [[evil]])
# [[goods]], [[property]]
#* {{quote-book|ru|author= w:Lazar Lagin|year= 1972|origyear= 1955, 1938|title= lw:ru:Старик Хоттабыч|chapter= Беспокойный вечер|page= 46
|newversion= English translation based on|translator2= Faina Solasko|title2= The Old Genie Hottabych|chapter2= A Troubled Evening|year2= 1960|page2= 54
|text= — Я превращу в пыль все товары, и все столы, и всё оборудование этой презренной лавки!<br>— Ты с ума сошёл! — вконец возмутился Волька.— Ведь это государственное добро, старая ты '''балда'''!
|translation= “I’ll turn all the goods, all the tables and all the equipment of this despicable shop into dust!”<br>“You’re mad!” Volka said, really angry by now. “Don’t you know that’s government '''property''', you old dope!”}}
# [[stuff]]
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[green light]], [[consent]], [[permission]], the [[OK]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[комитет|Комите́т]] [[дать|дал]] '''добро́''' [[на]] [[пока́з]] [[новый|но́вого]] [[фильм|фи́льма]].|The committee has given the '''go-ahead''' for screening the new film.}}
# the name of the letter д in the ancient Slavonic or old Russian alphabet

